  "question": {
    "text": "Three rods of identical cross-sectional area and made from the same metal form the sides of an isosceles triangle <em><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ABC</mi></math></em> right angled at <em><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math></em>. The points <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>&nbsp;are maintained at temperatures <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mi>T</mi></math>, respectively, in the steady-state. Assuming that only heat conduction takes place, the temperature of the point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> is<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0088_7c39f1e7c9d9.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 144px; height: 123px;\" />"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>T</mi><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>T</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mfenced><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>T</mi><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "As T<sub>B</sub> &gt; T<sub>A</sub>, heat flows from <em>B</em> to <em>A</em> through both paths <em>BA</em> and <em>BCA</em>.<br />Rate of heat flow in BC = Rate of heat flow in CA<br /><br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>K</mi><mi>A</mi><mfenced><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mi>T</mi><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mtext>c</mtext></msub></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mi>l</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">KA</mtext><mfenced><mrow><msub><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">T</mtext><mtext>c</mtext></msub><mo>-</mo><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">T</mtext></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mi>l</mi></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br />Solving this, we get&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mtext>c</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <u><strong><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0088_dafadb9fed27.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 154px; height: 164px;\" /></strong></u>"
  }
}